Extracted verbatim from the package, nothing else:
  build/native/include/WebView2.h                     -> include/WebView2.h
  build/native/include/WebView2EnvironmentOptions.h   -> include/WebView2EnvironmentOptions.h
  build/native/x64/WebView2LoaderStatic.lib           -> lib/x64/WebView2LoaderStatic.lib
  LICENSE.txt                                         -> LICENSE.txt
  NOTICE.txt                                          -> NOTICE.txt

The static loader is deliberate. This DLL is injected into an arbitrary host
process, so a side-by-side WebView2Loader.dll cannot be relied on; the loader
code has to live inside shadowtrainer.dll itself. build.cmd fails the build if
`dumpbin /dependents` shows a WebView2Loader.dll import.

The WebView2 runtime itself is NOT vendored -- the evergeen runtime installed
machine-wide is used. See docs/WEBUI.md.
